+# Plan
+
+## 1. Tests
+
+- [ ] 1.1 `import "foo"` in a file named script.cjs fails to parse with acorn, espree and meriyah, with the script-goal error (tests/format/misc/errors/js/known-source-type/jsfmt.spec.js) [AC-1]
+- [ ] 1.2 `with(foo) {}` in module.mjs and `delete foo` in module.mJs fail with the strict-mode error of each parser (tests/format/misc/errors/js/known-source-type/jsfmt.spec.js) [AC-2]
+
+## 2. Fix
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Read the source type from the file extension: `.cjs` is a script, `.mjs` is a module, matched without case, anything else unknown (src/language-js/parse/utils/get-source-type.js)
+- [ ] 2.2 Parse with only that source type when it is known, and keep trying module then script when it is not (src/language-js/parse/acorn.js, espree.js, meriyah.js)
+- [ ] 2.3 Let babel use the same source type when no explicit one is given, and reject import and export in script code as the other parsers do (src/language-js/parse/babel.js)
+- [ ] 2.4 Take the combinations as one array (src/utils/try-combinations.js, src/language-js/parse/typescript.js)
